{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["In His image — of man, that is in the image of Elohim: angels. And do not wonder that the creation of the angels was not specified, for Moshe did not write here either angels or Gehinnom or the Account of the Chariot, but only things that we see in the world, which are mentioned in the Ten Commandments — for that reason the works of the six days were stated, as I explained above." "Male and female He created them — as Scripture explains immediately after: ״וַיִּקַּח אַחַת מִצַּלְעֹתָיו״ — a general statement, and afterward it specifies. And so I found in the Thirty-two Rules of R. Eliezer son of R. Yosi HaGelili that he derived from this very verse the principle of a general statement followed by specification."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:17:35.063305973Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}